Written by hand for this repository on 2026-11-19 (CC0 1.0: no rights
reserved), for unit m8-i (settings from another design, properties
addendum 6.3 and 17; ledger row M8). The design whose setup settings.read
reads into settings-to; it is staged by the e2e, never opened.

settings-from.kicad_pro differs from KiCad's defaults in every section that
travels: a net class HV (0.5 mm clearance, 0.4 mm track, red, pattern HV*);
a component class POWER on REFERENCE U* with sheet classes on; a tuning
profile "USB 90R" (differential, 90 ohm, In2.Cu between In1.Cu and In3.Cu);
board severities (silk_overlap and lib_footprint_mismatch ignored,
track_dangling an error); ERC severities (pin_not_connected a warning,
similar_labels ignored) and two pin map cells; text and graphics defaults
(silk and copper text sizes, dimension precision 2); the apply-to-footprint
switches of the formatting on; zone defaults hatched (0.5 mm bars, 0.8 mm
gaps, 45 degrees, 0.6 mm clearance); constraints (0.15 mm clearance and
track, 0.45 mm via, 0.3 mm hole clearance); predefined tracks, vias and
diff pairs; teardrops on with a length ratio of 0.6 and on track ends;
tuning pattern spacing 1.2 mm and diff pair amplitude 1.5 mm; text variable
REV = C; bus alias ADDR (A0 to A3); BOM preset "Assembly" and format preset
"Semicolons"; annotation by Y (sort order 1), first free after a number
(method 1), from 100, designators reused; schematic formatting (dash ratio
8, gap 4, line 8 mils, text 60 mils, label ratio 0.375, offset 0.15,
intersheet references shown) and two field name templates, MPN and
Supplier. The ERC tables start from KiCad's own default tables (no creative
content) with those changes. Written as JSON in KiCad 10's own key names.

settings-from.kicad_pcb: six copper layers (In1.Cu a power plane named GND1,
In4.Cu a power plane), a stackup with ENIG finish, dielectric constraints,
an edge connector and edge plating, black mask, mask expansion 0.05 mm,
mask minimum width 0.1 mm, paste clearance -0.03 mm, soldermask bridges
allowed in footprints, a hatch offset of 0.5, 0.5 mm on In1.Cu, a dashed
line dash ratio of 6. Written by hand, loaded and saved by KiCad 10.0's own
board writer (kicad-cli pcb upgrade), then the zone_defaults block put back
by hand in the writer's own form: KiCad 10's parser reads a board file's
zone_defaults into the default zone settings and its writer writes the
board's own hatch offsets, so the save dropped it.

settings-from.kicad_dru: one rule, "HV spacing", a 1.5 mm clearance on the
net class HV.

Checked with kicad/kicad:10.0 before commit: pcb drc read the board, the
project and the rules with no error; sch erc and sch export bom with
--preset Assembly --format-preset Semicolons read the project (three
columns, semicolons). The KiCad files carry no comment, so this file holds
their license.
